# oracle: pair_style body/rounded/polygon with friction (mu 0.3) and tangential and normal damping (c_n 0.1, c_t 0.2, delta_ua 0.5), two tilted rounded squares moving into each other with spin, fix nve/body, 100 steps: thermo pe ke etotal and the atom state
# Measured (engine vs native, max relative error): thermo 1.5e-12, per-atom state 3.4e-14. Without friction (mu 0) the native atom positions after 100 steps differ by about 1e-3, so the friction term is exercised.
# oracle-inputs: w50bc_tilted.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       2
atom_style      body rounded/polygon 1 6
atom_modify     map array
read_data       w50bc_tilted.data
set             atom 1 vx 0.5 vy 0.0 vz 0.0
set             atom 2 vx -0.5 vy 0.0 vz 0.0
pair_style      body/rounded/polygon 0.1 0.2 0.3 0.5 1.0
pair_coeff      * * 100 2
comm_modify     vel yes
fix             1 all nve/body
fix             2 all enforce2d
timestep        0.01
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal press pxx pyy pxy
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             100
